; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Rhythm Blocks
; CATEGORY: Music & Sound
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     rhythm, fractions, beats, drawing
; SUMMARY:  Shows whole, half, quarter and eighth notes as blocks of different widths and claps out rhythms built from them.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   In music, how long a note lasts matters as much as how high it
;   is. A whole note lasts 4 beats, a half note 2, a quarter note 1
;   and an eighth note half a beat. Each row on the screen is one bar
;   of 4 beats, built from blocks whose width is their length. As a
;   row is drawn, you hear it clapped.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run with the sound on and clap along. Make your own rhythm
;   by writing a list of the letters w h q e and giving it to ROW.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * beats as numbers: 4, 2, 1 and 0.5
;   * every row adds up to 4 beats, like fractions that make a whole
;   * CASE chooses a value by matching a word
;   * a short tick followed by silence makes a clap sound
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Write a row with eight eighth notes: [e e e e e e e e].
;   * Change :beat to make the whole program faster or slower.
;   * Use a different tone for half notes so you can hear them.
; ============================================================

make "beat 500        ; one beat is half a second

; How many beats each letter stands for.
to beats :letter
  output case :letter [[[w] 4] [[h] 2] [[q] 1] [[e] 0.5] [else 0]]
end

; Every kind of note has its own color, so they are easy to tell apart.
to note.color :letter
  output case :letter [[[w] 4] [[h] 14] [[q] 2] [[e] 1] [else 0]]
end

; One clap: a 40 millisecond click, then silence for the rest of the note.
to clap :b
  localmake "ms :b * :beat
  sound (list 900 40 0 :ms - 40)
end

; Draw a row of blocks starting at height :y and clap each block.
to row :pattern :y
  localmake "x -300
  foreach :pattern [
    localmake "w 150 * beats ?
    penup setxy :x :y setheading 0 pendown
    setpencolor 7
    filled note.color ? [repeat 2 [fd 60 rt 90 fd :w - 6 rt 90]]
    penup setxy :x + 6 :y + 20 pendown
    setpencolor 0
    label ?
    clap beats ?
    make "x :x + :w
  ]
end

clearscreen
hideturtle
setbackground [235 235 245]
setlabelheight 24
penup setxy -300 260 pendown
label [w = 4 beats   h = 2   q = 1   e = 1/2]
row [w] 170
row [h h] 100
row [q q q q] 30
row [e e e e e e e e] -40
row [q q h] -110
row [e e q e e q] -180
row [h e e q] -250
